WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.720
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.730
This paper is about interactively modeling
and editing climbing plants.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:15.660
This is one of my favorite kind of works:
mundane sounding topic, immaculate execution.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.690
There are so many cool things about this paper,
I don't even know where to start.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.010
But first, let's let's talk about the modeling
part.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:28.220
We can, for instance, plant a seed, and we
can not only have a look at how it grows as

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:34.520
time goes by, but we can also influence the
grow variability and shoot growth rates.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.150
Branches can be added and removed at will
at any point in time.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:43.370
We can also add attractors, regions that are
set to be more likely for the plant to grow

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.370
towards.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.000
With these techniques, we can easily create
any sort of artistic effect, be it highly

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.300
artificial looking vines and branches, or
some long forgotten object overgrown with

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.760
climbing plants.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.170
However, a model is just 3d geometry.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:04.780
What truly makes these models come alive is
animation, which is also executed with flying

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:05.780
colors.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:11.299
The animations created with this technique
are both biologically and physically plausible.

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:14.020
So what do these terms mean exactly?

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.689
Biologically plausible means that the plants
grow according to the laws of nature, and

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.930
physically plausible means that if we start
tugging at it, branches start moving, bending

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.049
and breaking according to the laws of physics.

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:31.720
Due to its responsive and interactive nature,
the applications of this technique are typically

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:37.630
in the domain of architectural visualization,
digital storytelling, or any sort of real-time

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.649
application.

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.450
And of course, the usual suspects, animated
movies and game developers can use this to

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.740
create more immersive digital environments
with ease.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:52.149
And don't forget about me, Károly, who would
happily play with this basically all day long.

